What is the maximum number of activation records of `f` that exist on the stack at the same time during the call `f(3)` ?

```c
int i = 1;
int a[3] = {0, 10, 20};   // a[1] = 10, a[2] = 20
void p(int x) { i = 2; x = x + 5; }
main() { p(a[i]); print(a[1], a[2]); }
```

What is printed under call by name?

```c
